  "query_preview": "..\nAn unstable weather pattern will bring scattered showers and \nisolated thunderstorms tonight for the Marianas, becoming numerous \nby tomorrow. Higher rainfall totals are expected tonight for Guam \nand decreasing northward due to proximity to Invest 97W. Starting \nMonday night, high-end scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms \nare possible for the rest of the week. As 97W shifts north and \nelongates, winds will turn from east-southeast to southwest by \nTuesday. If 97W manages to develop northeast of the Marianas from \nthe ongoing southerly wind burst near Chuuk, then stronger monsoonal\nwesterlies could occur over the Marianas. However, this remains \nunlikely and forecasted winds remain at 15 to 20 mph for now \nbeginning Tuesday.",
